## 5. Error Handling

- All error cases from previous assignments still apply.
- All PA3 similarity-related errors also apply to PA4 prediction.
- If there are fewer than two cooperative users, report an error.
- If `-p` is passed but there are no missing ratings (every song has been rated by every user), report an error.
- If the third argument is present and is not `-a`, `-u`, or `-p`, report an error.

---

## 6. Running the Program

The first argument is the input CSV file. The second argument is the output CSV file. The optional third argument selects the mode.

### Default Mode: Song Statistics

```bash
gradle run -q --args="'database/files/file2.csv' 'output.csv'"
```

### User Similarities: `-u`

```bash
gradle run -q --args="'database/files/file1.csv' 'similarity.csv' '-u'"
```

### Predictions: `-p`

```bash
gradle run -q --args="'database/files/file4.csv' 'user_predictions.csv' '-p'"
```

### Write Output to an Existing Directory

```bash
gradle run -q --args="'database/files/file3.csv' 'existing_folder/predictions.csv' '-p'"
```

**Do not hard-code input or output paths.**

The user must be able to choose which input CSV to read and the name and location of the output CSV.

Use the `String[] args` parameter in the `main` method to read command-line arguments.

Only one output file is created per run. The output's contents depend on whether `-u` or `-p` is supplied.

